    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d420-a1">

                <pb facs="0623" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg529"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 407.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rawicz to Mr. Breckinridge.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Warsaw</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to acknowledge yours of 26th ultimo,
                    in answer to mine of 18th (s. m.), and in answer to your communication of 2d
                    ultimo, in re Henry Topor (Baritsky), United States citizen detained here. I can
                    inform you now that he left for America already, with the assistance of his
                    relatives, what [which] was communicated to me by his sister-in-law, Mrs. Mary
                    Divorakowska, of this city.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph Rawicz</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
